+# My fork of Skola
+
+Modified by Eli King on 2026-11-17 for the AI-First Design Workshop.
+This is my fork of Skola, not official Skola. It is not endorsed by the maintainer.
+
+[Source for this fork](https://github.com/eli-w-king/skola).
+The original project is [Skola by h16nning and contributors](https://github.com/h16nning/skola).
+This version remains under [AGPL-3.0](LICENSE), without warranty. Keep the original license and notices.
+
+## Workshop changes
+
+- Removed Dexie Cloud initialization, configuration and sign-in/sync UI. The database name and local schema are unchanged. Cards stay in this browser.
+- Fixed GitHub Pages project paths, the PWA manifest and service-worker scope. Removed the upstream domain and legacy deploy scripts. The deployment still runs the tests.
+- Added source links, a dated modification note and agent guidance for work in your own fork.
+
+Before sharing your own fork, change the name, date and source URL in `src/workshop.ts` and this section. The deployed source link includes the Actions build commit. Do not remove upstream credit.
+
+## Run this fork
+
+Use Node 22.22.1 or a version verified for the workshop. pnpm is pinned; Corepack is not needed.
+
+```sh
+npx pnpm@10.28.2 install --frozen-lockfile
+npx pnpm@10.28.2 start
+npx pnpm@10.28.2 test
+npx pnpm@10.28.2 build
+```
+
+The dev script is `start`, not `dev`. `BASE_PATH` defaults to `/` locally. For a project site, build with `BASE_PATH=/skola/` (PowerShell: `$env:BASE_PATH="/skola/"`). Actions reads the path from Configure Pages. Keep hash routes such as `/skola/#/home`.
+
+Enable Actions in your own fork, set Pages to GitHub Actions, and deploy only reviewed changes from `main`. Every pull request must target your own fork, not h16nning/skola or a prepared parent fork. Never sign in to Skola Cloud Sync.
+
+Use a new local profile for the workshop. If you have existing Skola data, export it before changing this build. This patch is not a migration from an authenticated sync account.
+
+## Original project README
+
 # Skola
 _Note: Skola is still in early-ish development. Expect bugs, missing features, and breaking changes. Feedback is very welcome!_
 
